/-!
# Binary MS core rigidity: proved intrinsic reductions

This entry point currently supplies the genuine binary MS inputs and their
component and conjugation-quotient reductions. The faithful central FF-module
excludes the full automorphism image, giving an actual compatible quotient
isomorphism J/O₂(J) ≃ SL₃(2) and its faithful binary FF-representation.
The intrinsic moving omega-center is nontrivial and has at least eight
elements, by MS3 and perfectness. Its upper bound and relative index remain open.
The numerical conclusion
`|Z([O₂(J),L])| ≤ 32 ∨ |[O₂(J),L]| = 64` still requires the binary local
rigidity argument of MS93. None of the reductions assumes that conclusion
or asserts the exhaustiveness of C.1.34.
The numerical assembly from elementary models is separately conditional;
the abelian-core and nonabelian-center model hypotheses remain to be proved.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004), C.1.31–34,
printed pp.135–137.
-/
